{
  "description": "A diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that inspects the actual trained recommender through a stable SASRec-compatible interface. It returns diagnostic metrics and their definitions while respecting the benchmark’s data and evaluation constraints.",
  "motivation": "Support model diagnosis and iterative improvement without fabricating unavailable attributes, accessing hidden test data, or changing the common evaluation protocol.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device) and run_full_diagnosis(train_loader). Use view.model as the trained nn.Module and adapt probes to architecture changes through item_emb, log2feats, and predict_score. Training batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B × L. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; treat review content, ratings, commercial attributes, and simulator traits as unavailable. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for 20 real training users, five per category. Select models using macro-average validation HR@10 across all four categories under the pinned evaluator.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    init(view, device):\n        retain view and device\n\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        set view.model to evaluation mode\n        disable gradients\n        inspect batches using architecture-compatible probes\n        compute supported diagnostics from observed data\n        mark unsupported diagnostics as unavailable\n        restore model training state\n        return metrics, metric_definitions\n\nFor simulator input:\n    recommend from the full catalog excluding observed items\n    use five real training users per category\n\nFor model selection:\n    use pinned macro-average validation HR@10",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines a stable diagnostic interface with explicit observability constraints and a shared recommendation benchmark.",
    "negative": "Describes an integration contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm or diagnostic method."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Can support comparable diagnostics across architectures and guide subsequent model improvements.",
    "negative": "Its usefulness depends on implementing informative probes; the description provides no evidence of improved recommendation accuracy."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 4,
    "positive": "The required interface, batch shapes, available inputs, and selection metric are clearly specified.",
    "negative": "Architecture changes require careful probe adaptation, and full-catalog recommendation must handle masking and computational cost."
  }
}
